  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5bb8abeb8477f3d47aac6a4d0e488fcf, type: 3}
  m_Name: EN
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp-firstpass::Daniel.Master.DialogueData
  DialogueNumber: 100
  Language: EN
  Lines:
  - Great. To help you know where you are even in enclosed spaces, there are three
    types of sounds.
  - When you run into a wall, you'll hear this sound.
  - When you walk along a wall, you'll hear this sound.
  - When there's a hallway to your left or right, you'll hear the sound of wind in
    your left or right ear.
  - One last thing.
  - When you're near an object you can interact with, this sound will play as long
    as you can interact with it.
  - On your right side in the back you have two buttons. Press the one in the front
    to interact
  - You are now in a room with an exit. Find the door you can interact with, then
    press the right button.
